Source. These are machine readings of line images from the Տօնացոյց
(Tonatsoyts), Jerusalem, 1915, which is in the public domain. This license
covers the readings, not the 1915 text.

What is here, and the terms of the model that produced each file. The whole
directory is offered under CC BY-NC 4.0, the most restrictive of these terms:

  - tess-calfa-n*:        Tesseract 5 with Calfa's `hye-calfa-n`
                          (https://github.com/calfa-co/hye-tesseract), CC BY-NC 4.0
  - paddle-calfa-tiny*:   PaddleOCR with Calfa's `paddle-calfa-tiny`
                          (https://github.com/calfa-co/hye-paddle), CC BY-NC 4.0
  - tess-grabar:          our fine-tune of `hye-calfa-n` (a derivative, so
                          CC BY-NC 4.0)
  - trocr-ft:             our fine-tune of Microsoft TrOCR (MIT)
  - surya:                Surya (Datalab, https://github.com/datalab-to/surya),
                          weights under a modified AI Pubs Open RAIL-M licence
  - dots-mocr:            dots.mocr (rednote-hilab), MIT
  - gemini-*, corr-gemini-*: Google Gemini API output (machine readings and
                          corrections)
  - *+rules:              the file above, after a deterministic orthography
                          rule from this repository

Credit for the Calfa readings: "OCR by Calfa (hye-calfa-n, paddle-calfa-tiny)."
When reusing this material, credit grabar-ocr (Andy Ylitalo) and Calfa.
